<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Telavi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Telavi is a town in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, the main centre of Kakheti, on the slopes above the Alazani valley. It was a seat of the kings of Kakheti-Hereti in the 11th century and later of the Kingdom of Kakheti, and the palace of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erekle-ii">Erekle II</a>, built in the 18th century, survives within its walled royal compound. It lies at the heart of Georgia's chief wine region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/telavi.jpg" alt="Telavi" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jelger Groeneveld · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rustaveli_Street,_Telavi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
